{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120792","id":3966492188,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7sa94c","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120792","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120792.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120792.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120792","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120792/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120792/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120792/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/f03e744178d4dce8d607211e8c5cd8e123dcb5f5","number":120792,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix godot crash in SpriteFrames in the AnimatedSprite2D and 3D","user":{"login":"Thiago-Weiss","id":137117035,"node_id":"U_kgDOCCw9aw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/137117035?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thiago-Weiss","html_url":"https://github.com/Thiago-Weiss","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thiago-Weiss/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thiago-Weiss/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thiago-Weiss/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thiago-Weiss/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thiago-Weiss/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thiago-Weiss/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thiago-Weiss/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thiago-Weiss/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thiago-Weiss/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nFixes a crash that occurs when editing an `AnimatedSprite2D` or `AnimatedSprite3D` after its `SpriteFrames` resource has been cleared in the Inspector.\r\n\r\nThe editor plugin remains active because the selected node is still focused, even though its `SpriteFrames` reference becomes `nullptr`. This leaves the plugin in an invalid state where the user can still interact with it and causing a crash.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Bug lifecycle\r\n\r\nThe `SpriteFramesEditorPlugin` handles both:\r\n\r\n- `AnimatedSprite2D`\r\n- `AnimatedSprite3D`\r\n- `SpriteFrames`\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nbool SpriteFramesEditorPlugin::handles(Object *p_object) const {\r\n    ...\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhen an `AnimatedSprite2D` or `AnimatedSprite3D` node is selected, the editor opens the `SpriteFramesEditor` plugin.\r\n\r\nDuring initialization (`_fetch_sprite_node()`), the plugin checks whether the currently selected node references the same `SpriteFrames` resource. If it does, it stores the node and connects to the `sprite_frames_changed` signal.\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nvoid SpriteFramesEditor::_fetch_sprite_node() {\r\n    ...\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe issue appears when the `SpriteFrames` property is cleared from the Inspector.\r\n\r\nAt this point:\r\n\r\n- the selected node remains selected;\r\n- the editor plugin stays open;\r\n- the edited `SpriteFrames` resource becomes `nullptr`.\r\n\r\nSince the plugin is not closed immediately, its UI remains interactive while referencing an invalid resource. Interacting with it can then trigger a crash.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\n\r\nThe plugin already connects to the node's `sprite_frames_changed` signal during initialization.\r\n\r\nWhen the resource changes, `_edit()` is called:\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nvoid SpriteFramesEditor::_edit() {\r\n    if (!animated_sprite) {\r\n        return;\r\n    }\r\n    edit(animated_sprite->call(\"get_sprite_frames\"));\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhen `get_sprite_frames()` now returns `nullptr`, `edit(nullptr)` is called.\r\n\r\nInstead of only clearing the edited `SpriteFrames` reference and leaving the editor open, this change ensures the plugin exits the editing state, preventing the user from interacting with an invalid resource.\r\n\r\nAs a result, the stale editor state is removed before it can lead to a crash.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Demonstration\r\nA video showing both the crash and the fix is attached below.\r\n\r\n[A video showing both the crash and the fix is attached below.](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/58f145c1-e972-4fdb-b896-2777a1f8f917)\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Related discussion\r\n\r\nA related discussion about a different approach can be found here:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112723## ","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"topic:editor","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1327318271,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMzI3MzE4Mjcx","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/crash","name":"crash","description":"","color":"885544","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":15520464,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A7NLQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/25","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25/labels","number":25,"state":"open","title":"4.8","description":"","creator":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo